<!--
  BlockML Definition — aggregation member meta-model type

  FQN: org.blockml.bml.definition.AggregationDefinition
  See docs/12_bom_object_model.md — AggregationDefinition · 02_mbml.md — Aggregations.
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/schema/block"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/schema/block https://blockml.org/schemas/core/block.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:def="org.blockml.bml.definition"
  xmlns:bml="http://blockml.org/schema/bml">

  <idea>An owned collection member — Block instances or type references depending on aggregation type.</idea>

  <documentation>Describes a Block member representing an owned collection. The aggregation type
    attribute selects payload semantics:

    • Plain Block type (for example core:Block[]) — composition ownership. Children are Block
      instances with optional nested composition element, member values, and bml:id.
    • TypeReference(T) (for example core:TypeReference(core:Block)[]) — type-reference list.
      Children are direct Block references (element name = FQN via xmlns prefix). No member values,
      bml:id, bml:version (unless documented otherwise), composition, or default="true".

    See org.blockml.bml.core.TypeReference. Rendered as a child element inside the aggregations
    container; the XML element name is the aggregation name (bml:xml="${ #this.name }"). An optional
    XML prefix on the element name supplies the member namespace — resolved via xmlns to BOM
    namespace; unprefixed elements use the default namespace (empty string). Member identity is
    (resolvedNamespace, localName). Maps to BOM AggregationDefinition (kind: "aggregation") with
    type expression (including TypeReference applications), cardinality (from type multiplicity),
    optional default flag (instance aggregations only), and optional nested composition template.
    When exactly one instance aggregation on a Block is marked default="true", bare top-level
    composition on the Block definition is sugar for filling that aggregation. Scalar member fields
    (type, default) follow org.blockml.bml.definition.MemberDefinition placement rules — element
    preferred on definitions, attribute preferred on Block instances. Structured composition remains
    a child element on instance aggregations only. Composition instance ID reachability for
    bml:id references is controlled by this aggregation member's visibility (inherited from
    org.blockml.bml.definition.MemberDefinition) — public aggregations export ids for cross-document
    {EnclosingBlockFQN}::{id} references; protected limits reach to the declaring Block and its child
    Blocks; private limits reach to the declaring Block only. Service binding on composition children
    bml:bean and bml:scope on Block instances — not aggregation member fields.</documentation>

  <references>
    <see file="12_bom_object_model.md">
      AggregationDefinition BOM structure and CompositionTemplate.
    </see>
    <see file="02_mbml.md">
      Aggregations, composition placement, and default aggregation rules.
    </see>
    <see block="core:Block">
      Required branch for aggregation payload types.
    </see>
    <see block="core:TypeReference">
      Type-reference aggregation marker — TypeReference(T) vs instance Block[].
    </see>
  </references>

  <name>AggregationDefinition</name>
  <type>
    <def:AggregationDefinition />
  </type>
  <baseType>
    <def:MemberDefinition />
  </baseType>
  <properties>
    <type type="FullyQualifiedName(core:Block, core:TypeReference)" bml:xml="element|attribute">
      <documentation>Aggregation payload type (TypeExpression). Instance collections use a plain Block
        FQN with multiplicity — for example core:Block[], core:Block[0..n], core:Block[1..1].
        Type-reference collections wrap the payload constraint in TypeReference — for example
        core:TypeReference(core:Block)[], core:TypeReference(core:Language)[1..1]. The validator
        unwraps TypeReference(T) to detect type-reference mode; each child must satisfy
        satisfiesTypeBound(fqn, T). Required on new aggregation declarations; may be omitted when
        filling an inherited aggregation (partial override). On definitions, element form is
        preferred; on Block instances, attribute form is preferred.</documentation>
    </type>
    <default bml:xml="element|attribute">
      <value>false</value>
      <documentation>When true, marks this aggregation as the primary/default composition target for
        the enclosing Block — instance aggregations only (forbidden when type is TypeReference(T)).
        Tooling and render targets may use it when composition placement is ambiguous. At most one
        default="true" aggregation per Block. Maps to BOM AggregationDefinition.default.
        Default false.</documentation>
    </default>
    <composition type="Composition" bml:xml="element">
      <documentation>Optional nested composition template filling this instance aggregation on the
        Block definition. Forbidden when aggregation type is TypeReference(T). Rendered as a
        composition child element inside the aggregation member element. Maps to BOM
        AggregationDefinition.composition (CompositionTemplate). May be omitted on override
        declarations that only refine metadata. On Block instances, aggregation content is opened
        inline without a composition wrapper — see docs/02_mbml.md — Composition.</documentation>
    </composition>
  </properties>

  <subBlocks>
    <block>
      <idea>Composition template nested inside an aggregation member on a Block definition.</idea>

      <documentation>Describes the composition element on an aggregation member declaration.
        Rendered as composition with optional bml:with directives and a tree of composition child
        nodes (Block instances and bml:container virtual containers). Maps to BOM
        CompositionTemplate { aggregationName (from enclosing aggregation member name), directives,
        children }. Instance ID reachability is determined by the enclosing aggregation member's
        visibility — not by attributes on the composition element. Standalone composition outside an
        aggregation member element is invalid (BML_STANDALONE_COMPOSITION). Declared as the
        composition property on org.blockml.bml.definition.AggregationDefinition.</documentation>

      <name>Composition</name>
      <baseType>
        <core:Entity />
      </baseType>
      <bml:xml>composition</bml:xml>
    </block>
  </subBlocks>

</block>
